# OneWoW Suite Changelog

`CHANGELOG.md` is the user-facing release note uploaded to CurseForge (via
`bin/release_curseforge.py`). Keep the dialect simple: the uploader only
supports `#` / `##` / `###`, `-` lists (2-space nest), `---` rules, blank
lines, and basic `` `code` `` / `*em*` / `**bold**`.

## Document skeleton

Preserve this order and heading style:

```markdown
# OneWoW Suite Changelog

## Feature Area
- User-facing bullet

---

# Notes
## Optional subsection
- Cross-cutting or deferred notes

---

# AddonName
## Feature Area
- User-facing bullet

---

*No user-facing changes this release for Trackers, Shopping List, …*

---

- **Last Updated**: Mon DD, YYYY
```

1. **Title** — always `# OneWoW Suite Changelog` (H1).
2. **Suite-wide sections** — `##` under the title for core / shared features
   (e.g. Overlay System). Separate major blocks with a lone `---` line.
3. **`# Notes`** — optional H1 block for cross-cutting notes that are not a
   load-unit section.
4. **Per-addon sections** — one H1 per load unit (`# AltTracker`, `# Catalog`,
   `# QoL`, `# Bags`, …). Use `##` for feature areas inside an addon
   (`## Fixes`, `## Vendor Panel`). If an addon has only a flat list, bullets
   may sit directly under the H1 (no empty `##`).
5. **No-changes footer** — italic sentence listing every suite unit with
   nothing user-facing this release:
   `*No user-facing changes this release for A, B, or C.*`
   Omit units that already have an H1 section above. Use “or” before the last
   name. Drop the whole italic line only when every unit has a section.
6. **Metadata** — after a final `---`, exactly one bold-label bullet:
   - `**Last Updated**`: human date (`Jul 16, 2026`)

## Writing rules

- Write for players, not developers: what changed in-game, not file/API names.
- Prefer short `-` bullets; nest with exactly two spaces (`  -`) for sub-options.
- **Include** player-felt changes: visible UI/behavior/settings **and** experiential
  wins players feel but may not “see” (performance, snappiness, reliability —
  e.g. bank opens faster). Player-facing bugfixes count even when the UI looks the same.
- **Exclude** pure internals with no felt difference (rename, comment/doc-only,
  formatting, agent-context/rules, dead-code cleanup with identical behavior).
- Do not invent sections for units with no user-facing change — put them in the
  italic footer instead.
- Do not add changelog noise to Lua comments; this file is the release record.
- LF only (repo-wide). No tables, HTML, or unsupported markdown.

## Downstream mirrors

`CHANGELOG.md` is the source of truth for the in-progress release. After adding
or changing player-facing bullets, keep these in sync (**changelog → others**;
never the reverse):

1. **`wiki/Release-Notes.md` → `## Current`** — full mirror of this file’s body
   under Current on the **index** (heading demotion + wiki chrome). Shipped
   versions are summaries + links to `Release-Notes-<TOCVersion>.md`. Format and
   release archive: `onewow-wiki` / `OneWoW-Wiki.mdc`.
2. **What’s New** — concise in-game highlights derived from this changelog (below).

At CurseForge release: move Current into `wiki/Release-Notes-<TOCVersion>.md`,
add an index summary + link, reset this file’s skeleton (unless the release bot
already cleared it), and clear or rebuild What’s New for the next cycle (see
wiki release-notes section).

## What’s New

`OneWoW/Core/WhatsNewData.lua` drives the in-game What’s New dialog (Home link +
login auto-show). It is a **short summary** of the current CHANGELOG cycle — not
a second full changelog.

- **Reassess** whenever this changelog changes; **edit only when** the highlight
  set or wording should change (new high-impact item, merge into an existing
  body, drop/replace a weaker item, or leave alone if the bullet is minor).
- **Count:** up to **7** `{ titleKey, bodyKey }` entries — fewer is fine (3–5 is
  normal when the cycle is small). Never pad to fill 7.
- **Titles:** reuse an existing player-facing locale key when it fits
  (`HOME_TAB`, `MAIL`, …); otherwise add `WHATS_NEW_H_*_TITLE`.
- **Bodies:** dedicated `WHATS_NEW_H_*_BODY` strings — player voice, one short
  paragraph each.
- **Locales:** any key add/change → `onewow-locale-workflow` (all 11 locales).
- **Lifetime:** same cycle as this file. Players see the highlights shipped in
  their TOC; after release reset, rebuild for the next cycle as CHANGELOG grows.
